  "diagnosis": "The previous attempt failed validation due to numerical error (absolute difference up to 4.6e-5, relative up to 0.05, while tolerances are 2e-5 and 2e-4 respectively). The root cause is that the mean and variance were computed using only the first BLOCK columns, not over the entire row for arbitrary N>BLOCK. In the blockwise loop, only the first chunk is used for stats, which is incorrect for remaining columns. Layernorm requires mean and variance over all N elements of the row.",
  "outcome": "incorrect-numerics-stats-coverage",
  "next_step": "Repair by computing the mean and variance over the full row: accumulate sum and squared sum across all chunks in a blockwise loop, then compute mean/variance/scaling. Only after that, loop again to apply the affine normalization to each chunk using the correct row stats. Ensure all reduction identities and masking are handled, and that all loads and stores are masked for N."
